# Oral and Extreme Deployment Protocol

> [!abstract] Owns high-risk, time-boxed tools.
> This note exists to stop harsh compounds from becoming "normal background." It governs orals, tren, insulin, aggressive thyroid/stimulant overlap, and exotic final-shred blends.

> [!danger] Boundary
> Not a prescription. This protocol is mostly a blocker and stop-rule system. Any deployment requires clinician review, current labs, a dated start/stop plan, and written exit criteria.

## Owned Products

- Oral AAS / androgen stress: [[Oxandrolone (Anavar) (10mg×100tab) — kohohpharma]], YK-11 offers, stanozolol offers
- Tren lane: [[Trenbolone Acetate Acro (100mg-ml ×10ml) — beligaspharmacy Intl|Trenbolone Acetate]]
- Thyroid/stimulant overlap: [[Levothyroxine (T4) (50mcg×100tab) — shopee-china]], [[Cytolin (25mcg×100tab) — kohohpharma]], [[Clenbuterol (40mcg×100tab) — kohohpharma]]
- Insulin lane: [[Humalog insulin lispro (1500IU) — anabolicpharmacist]], [[Humalog Mix25 KwikPen (100IU-ml 3ml ×5pen) — anabolicpharmacist]]
- Extreme blends: [[Super Helios (20ml) — aminotech]], [[Super Shredder (20ml) — aminotech]]
- Support products: [[TUDCA (250mg×60tab) — iHerb]], [[NAC (600mg×180tab) — iHerb]], [[P5P (Pyridoxal-5-Phosphate) (50mg×240cap) — iHerb]], [[Calcium D-Glucarate (500mg×120tab) — iHerb]], [[DIM (300mg×120tab) — iHerb]]

## Entry Criteria

All must be true before any high-risk window:

- Exact reason for the tool is written: strength retention, terminal cut, specific androgen role, or supervised glucose use.
- Start date, stop date, max duration, and exit criteria are written before the first dose/injection.
- Baseline BP/HR, sleep, CBC, CMP, lipids, renal markers, liver markers, and glucose risk are reviewed.
- Support protocols are active: [[Year-Round Shield]], [[Lipid Management Protocol]], [[Renal & Hepatic Support Protocol]], [[Blood Pressure & Fluid Escalation Protocol]].
- The user has a recovery/downshift plan after the window.

## Hard Blocks

Do not deploy if:

- Labs are missing or already bad.
- BP/HR is uncontrolled.
- Sleep is unstable before adding stimulants, tren, or thyroid.
- The plan includes insulin without medical supervision, glucose monitoring, carb plan, and hypoglycemia rescue plan.
- The tool is being added because diet/training adherence is poor.
- The stop date is not written.

## Compound-Specific Guardrails

- **Oral AAS:** lipid damage and liver-marker monitoring are mandatory. Support products do not make a bad lipid panel acceptable.
- **Tren lane:** neuropsychological, sleep, BP, prolactin/E2-context, and relationship/function monitoring are part of the protocol, not afterthoughts. Use [[Neuroprotection Protocol (Tren)]].
- **Thyroid lane:** thyroid hormones are not casual fat-loss agents. Watch tremor, heat intolerance, anxiety, insomnia, HR, and cardiac symptoms.
- **Clen/stimulant lane:** do not stack adrenergic load without BP/HR and sleep control.
- **Insulin lane:** not operational here. Requires a separate supervised medical plan due to hypoglycemia and hypokalemia risk.
- **Extreme blends:** no blend is approved just because it exists in a vendor list. Require ingredient clarity, route clarity, and stop rules.

## Monitoring

- Daily during active window: BP/HR, sleep, mood, anxiety/irritability, temperature/heat tolerance, hydration, cramps, appetite, training quality.
- Weekly or phase-dependent: bodyweight, waist, photos, performance, side-effect log.
- Labs: CBC, CMP, lipids, liver markers, renal markers; CK if severe muscle symptoms; glucose/ketones if glucose-risk tools are active.
- Cross-check: [[Lipid Management Protocol]], [[Renal & Hepatic Support Protocol]], [[Blood Pressure & Fluid Escalation Protocol]], [[Glucose & Insulin Sensitivity Protocol]], [[Neuroprotection Protocol (Tren)]].

## Red Flags

Stop and seek review for chest pain, fainting, severe palpitations, severe anxiety/insomnia, aggression or depressive crash, jaundice, dark urine, severe abdominal pain, severe muscle pain with dark urine, hypoglycemia symptoms, confusion, shortness of breath, neurological symptoms, or uncontrolled BP/HR.

## Exit Criteria

Exit when the planned stop date arrives, when target benefit is achieved, or when any marker or symptom crosses a stop rule. A high-risk window does not extend itself because performance feels good.

## Stock Math

- High-risk products are projected by **dated window**, not annual use.
- Support products are projected with the same start/stop window and post-window lab plan.
- Keep oral AAS, thyroid, clen/stimulant, insulin, and blends in separate stock categories so they cannot be normalized by accident.
- Any leftover stock remains reserve; it does not imply another deployment.

